  (text "Q6\nSTL059N4S8AG\n40V 0.59mohm" (at 152 84 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "common source (TS)\n(gates lifted by driver)" (at 100 96 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "U5 INA210 gain 200\nU6 LM311 50mV hyst\nINA210 across Rsns_sw\nLM311 -> gate driver\n(ICs on +5V)" (at 122 102 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "TWO N-CHANNEL BIDIRECTIONAL SWITCH + IDEAL-DIODE CONTROLLER:\nQ5/Q6 in series, sources tied (common-source = TS). Drains to CTRL_BLACK_IN\nand TRACK_POS. Opposing body diodes block both directions when off; both channels\nconduct (low Rds) when on. Controlled as an ideal diode by U5 INA210 + U6 LM311 (+5V).\nGATE DRIVE OPEN ITEM: gates must be lifted above the 0-16V BLACK common source; the\nTPS1212 did this with an internal charge pump - the ideal diode needs a discrete high-side\ndriver / charge pump (from WHITE, +12V_RAIL) gated by the LM311 output." (at 15 120 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "IDEAL-DIODE REVERSE BLOCK (replaces TPS1212-Q1):\nU5 INA210 (gain 200) senses across Rsns_sw (~1mohm). U6 LM311 compares its output to a\nthreshold (~0.16A) with ~50mV hysteresis; on reverse current LM311 turns the gate driver off\n-> body diodes block. Reverse response ~2us (sim - validate with real INA210+LM311 models).\nThe LM311 output doubles as the MCU brake-detect on PA6 (was TPS1212 I_DIR).\nNO I2t/SCP/IMON: TPS1212 automotive protection is dropped (open item) - accepted as the reverse\nevent (brake-contact closure) is brief, but the pass FETs lose their own fault protection.\nCM at the shunt must stay < 26V (INA210 limit; was 73V on the TPS1212)." (at 15 145 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "INSERTION DROP at 40A:\n2 x 0.59mohm FET (47mV) + Rsns_sw ~1mohm (40mV) = ~87mV.\nRsns_sw is a drop-vs-sense-accuracy knob: ~1mohm gives the sim +/-0.16A reverse threshold;\na smaller shunt = lower drop but coarser threshold. The back-to-back pair is still required\nfor true bidirectional blocking (a single FET body diode conducts the blocked direction)." (at 15 172 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "PB3: now a free GPIO. The ideal diode has no enable input; the TPS1212 EN/UVLO is gone." (at 15 196 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
)
